{"title":"Career Roadmap — Quality Controller","role":"Quality Controller","summary":"A Dairy Quality Controller ensures that milk and dairy products meet required standards for safety, composition, microbiological quality, processing parameters, shelf life and regulatory compliance. The role covers raw-milk testing, process control, laboratory analysis, hygiene, HACCP, quality systems and finished-product inspection.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Dairy Technology"},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"Very High — Dairy Technology directly prepares students for quality-control roles in dairy plants, food-processing companies, laboratories and regulatory environments."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Dairy chemistry, microbiology, processing, laboratory testing and food safety"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Quality Controller → Quality Assurance Officer → Senior Quality Executive"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"QA/QC Manager, Food Safety Manager, Quality Systems Specialist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Head of Quality, Food Safety Director, Dairy Quality/Technical Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Chemistry, biology, mathematics, physics and food science"},{"text":"Understand milk composition and basic laboratory methods"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Dairy chemistry, microbiology, processing and engineering"},{"text":"Perform raw-milk and process testing"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Quality control, food safety, HACCP and dairy microbiology"},{"text":"Manage dairy quality parameters"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"QA systems, audits, regulatory compliance and quality analytics"},{"text":"Build a complete dairy quality-management system"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Dairy & Food Science Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chemistry"},{"text":"Biology"},{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Food science fundamentals"},{"text":"Microbiology fundamentals"},{"text":"Dairy terminology"},{"text":"Laboratory safety"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Excel"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand milk composition:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water"},{"text":"Fat"},{"text":"Protein"},{"text":"Lactose"},{"text":"Minerals"},{"text":"Vitamins"},{"text":"Somatic cells"},{"text":"Microbial load"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mini-project"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare the quality characteristics of different milk samples using:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pH"},{"text":"Acidity"},{"text":"Fat"},{"text":"Protein"},{"text":"Solids-not-fat"},{"text":"Density"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Dairy Processing & Laboratory Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dairy chemistry"},{"text":"Dairy microbiology"},{"text":"Milk processing"},{"text":"Pasteurisation"},{"text":"Homogenisation"},{"text":"Cream separation"},{"text":"Fermentation"},{"text":"Refrigeration"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Cleaning and sanitation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Laboratory skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pH testing"},{"text":"Acidity testing"},{"text":"Fat analysis"},{"text":"Protein analysis"},{"text":"Total solids"},{"text":"Microbial testing"},{"text":"Adulteration screening"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a Milk Quality Testing & Classification System that categorises samples based on quality parameters."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Quality Control Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"h","text":"Raw-Milk Quality"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Milk reception"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Acidity"